&lt;p&gt;I am a data scientist and engineering manager at &lt;a href=&quot;https://posit.co/&quot;&gt;Posit PBC&lt;/a&gt; where I work on tools for data science like &lt;a href=&quot;https://github.com/posit-dev/positron&quot;&gt;Positron&lt;/a&gt;, &lt;a href=&quot;https://vetiver.posit.co/&quot;&gt;vetiver&lt;/a&gt;, and others. My last name is pronounced SILL-GHEE (two syllables, short &lt;code&gt;i&lt;/code&gt;, hard &lt;code&gt;g&lt;/code&gt;). I love making beautiful charts, the statistical programming language R, Jane Austen, black coffee, and red wine.&lt;/p&gt; 
&lt;p&gt;In school, I studied physics and astronomy; I worked in academia (teaching and doing research) and ed tech before moving into data science in 2015 and discovering R. I am an author, an international speaker, and a real-world practitioner focusing on data analysis and machine learning. I have written books with my collaborators about &lt;a href=&quot;https://www.tidytextmining.com/&quot;&gt;text mining&lt;/a&gt;, &lt;a href=&quot;https://smltar.com/&quot;&gt;supervised machine learning for text&lt;/a&gt;, and &lt;a href=&quot;https://www.tmwr.org/&quot;&gt;modeling with tidy data principles&lt;/a&gt; in R.&lt;/p&gt; 
&lt;p&gt;I live in Salt Lake City, UT, with my husband, three kids, and two cats.&lt;/p&gt; 
